Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:36:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings, skin.estuary: the spline darkens the shadows of a
 shot too

The help of "Tone mapping curve" (Dolby Vision as HDR10 mapped to the
display, #39845 and the skin's #31785) said that libplacebo's spline
darkens the middle tones of a shot to keep its contrast. It darkens its
shadows as well, without taking them to black. Measured on Mesa's zink with
the bridge, mapped to a display of 600 cd/m2 (P3) against the picture as
it is, below 1 cd/m2: a ramp of PQ codes comes out 35 % darker (up to 21
codes of 1023 lower), a profile 5 chart 45 %, profile 5 film pictures 15 %
and profile 7 FEL pictures 10 %, no pixel at black; with BT.2390, the
default, the same ramp comes out as it is (no code off). The help now says
so, in English and in the three Spanish languages. Nothing else changes.
